                        "sense_id": "c04f19d3-e34a-3dd3-8512-49ebfc630b46",
                        "entry_id": "78c66e14-100e-387e-9869-70ce46447049",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a peremptory manner; in a commanding tone, brooking no delay."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c5279a9-6b27-471a-acbd-dc35dc962367",
                                "sense_id": "c04f19d3-e34a-3dd3-8512-49ebfc630b46",
                                "text": "He was peremptorily summoned to see the commanding officer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f3c71f4-db3a-4eb4-8b25-9ad17a5c722d",
                                "sense_id": "c04f19d3-e34a-3dd3-8512-49ebfc630b46",
                                "text": "1597, Francis Bacon, Essays, New York: T.Y. Cromwell, 1901, LVII, \"Of Anger\", p. 233, https://archive.org/details/essaysoffrancisb00baco\n[…] that you doe not peremptorily break off, in any Businesse, in a Fitt of Anger: But howsoever you shew Bitternes, do not Act any thing, that is not Revocable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e39710b-67cd-4d9f-a15b-af70d9711a00",
                                "sense_id": "c04f19d3-e34a-3dd3-8512-49ebfc630b46",
                                "text": "I shall not peremptorily deny, that from most of such mixt bodies as partake either of animal or vegetable nature, there may by the help of the fire be actually obtained a determinate number […] of substances, worthy of differing denominations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7babbe5-4177-400d-b950-3cb31ee95f2c",
                                "sense_id": "c04f19d3-e34a-3dd3-8512-49ebfc630b46",
                                "text": "How have I offended you? Twice have I called this morning, and each time you have been peremptorily denied."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fcc6f34-12b0-47ad-b5d0-7f0f4491261c",
                                "sense_id": "c04f19d3-e34a-3dd3-8512-49ebfc630b46",
                                "text": "[…] the door-bell jingled peremptorily, and the girl left waiting on the table to go and answer it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "10bcaec4-ce8d-4d18-b0eb-b03c7fd0476f",
                                "sense_id": "c04f19d3-e34a-3dd3-8512-49ebfc630b46",
                                "text": "\"Never mind that!\" here peremptorily broke in the superior, his face altering with anger […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
